From e644d9ef03aedf77c386800c7d721e67c779e7fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Schuldesz <paulschuldesz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:26:27 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH v1 1/1] scsi: ufs: qcom: Power down the link during system
 suspend on Milos
To: Manivannan Sadhasivam <mani@kernel.org>,
    James E.J. Bottomley <James.Bottomley@HansenPartnership.com>,
    Martin K. Petersen <mkp@kernel.org>
Cc: linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-scsi@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

Milos (SM7635) has the same split UFS GDSC layout as SM8550/SM8650: one
GDSC for the host controller and a separate one for the QMP PHY. genpd
powers both off in the suspend_noirq phase, so the PHY state is lost.
Resuming with the link left in Hibern8 (the ufshcd default spm_lvl 3)
then fails on the Fairphone 6:

  ufshcd-qcom 1d84000.ufshc: pwr ctrl cmd 0x18 (DME_HIBERNATE_EXIT) failed, host upmcrs:0x5
  ufshcd-qcom 1d84000.ufshc: __ufshcd_wl_resume: hibern8 exit failed 5

followed by a full host and device reset.

The milos DT node lists "qcom,milos-ufshc" first but the driver only
matches the generic "qcom,ufshc" entry, which has no drvdata. Add a
milos entry with no_phy_retention set, as was done for SM8550/SM8650, so
the link and device are powered down (UFS_PM_LVL_5) during system
suspend. Milos reports LSDBS correctly, so the SM8550
UFSHCD_QUIRK_BROKEN_LSDBS_CAP quirk is not inherited.

Tested on the Fairphone 6 only so far as: writing spm_lvl=5 through
sysfs is accepted and reads back as POWERDOWN/OFF. A full system
suspend/resume cycle with this patch has not been run yet.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index fb5213bad4a6..44f8125e34e4 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -3042,12 +3042,25 @@ static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata = {
 	.no_phy_retention = true,
 };
 
+/*
+ * Milos (SM7635) uses the same split UFS_PHY_GDSC / UFS_MEM_PHY_GDSC layout as
+ * SM8550/SM8650 and likewise loses the PHY state when those GDSCs are powered
+ * off by genpd during system suspend, so the default spm_lvl 3 (link in
+ * Hibern8) fails with "hibern8 exit failed 5" on resume. Power the link down
+ * (UFS_PM_LVL_5) like SM8550/SM8650. LSDBS is reported correctly here, so
+ * the SM8550 BROKEN_LSDBS_CAP quirk is not inherited.
+ */
+static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_milos_drvdata = {
+	.no_phy_retention = true,
+};
+
 static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata = {
 	.vops = &ufs_hba_qcom_sa8255p_vops
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id ufs_qcom_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ufshc" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,milos-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_milos_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sa8255p-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata },
